#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# inner

#% text
# `inner(f, a, b)` gives the generalised inner product of vectors or matrices: the sums of `f` of corresponding elements.
# `inner(f, a, b, g)` combines with `g` in place of addition.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Vectors with the same head, a list or any other, contract alike; the level argument `k` contracts the k-th index of the first array with the first index of the second (the last index is the default).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
inner(mul, [a, b, c], [x, y, z])
#% output
#= a*x + b*y + c*z

#% cell
inner(mul, [[1, 2], [3, 4]], [5, 6])
#% output
#= [17, 39]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Another combination than the sum:

#% cell
inner(add, [1, 2], [3, 4], mul)
#% output
#= 24

#% subsection
# Options

#% cell
inner(s, f(1), f(2), t)
#% output
#= t(s(1, 2))

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `dot`, `outer`, `total`
